# ── Loadout deploy reasons ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These five were absent from the catalogue entirely, which is why the loadout
# screen could not assert them: an assertion against a key with no msgstr passes
# vacuously, because the key translates to ITSELF. They rendered as the raw
# constant. UPPERCASE, as the outcome chips are.

# --- loadout refusal reasons ---
# Keys referenced as constants by src/meta/loadout_view.gd (REASON_KEYS).
#
# HISTORY, kept because the three states are indistinguishable from the outside and
# that is the whole point of recording them. These keys were ABSENT from the
# catalogue entirely, existing only as GDScript constants, so no translation tool
# could see them. ea589a8 added the msgids with EMPTY msgstrs, which is the state
# the tooling is designed to report on. They are FILLED as of this commit. All
# three states return the key itself from translate(key) == key, so a count that
# measures CHANGE could not tell them apart -- and reported "0 untranslated" while
# the keys were missing. validate_i18n now reports PRESENCE separately from absence
# for exactly this reason; see _check_every_key_is_translated.
# ── Loadout refusal reasons, player-facing pt-BR ─────────────────────────
# The view (loadout_view.gd) carries each reason as a KEY and never as a composed
# literal -- its own rule, "a blocking reason as a KEY and never a composed
# literal", exists so the sentence belongs to the catalogue. It also builds no UI:
# it is the authority layer, and the reason reaches the player through whatever
# renders rows(). So these five msgstrs ARE the whole player-facing text, and a
# player reads them as a label on the offending item or slot, not as a sentence
# inside a longer sentence.
#
# SENTENCE CASE, and that is a decision with evidence rather than taste. The
# catalogue already has 18 ALL-CAPS msgstrs, but every one of them is a raid-feed
# STATUS STAMP (SOBREVIVEU, MORT0 EM ACAO, CENARIO CONCLUIDO, PAGA, SINALIZADOR),
# where the genre convention is a terse stamped token. The two nearest precedents
# for a UI LABEL are sentence case: "Active kit" -> "Equipamento ativo" and
# "Loadout selected" -> "Equipamento selecionado". All caps here would have been
# the wrong register: it would read as a status stamp in a feed, on a screen that
# is not a feed, and it is the shape a developer identifier takes -- which is
# exactly the failure the card names.
#
# Past participles, not imperatives or diagnoses. The screen says WHICH ITEM is
# the reason, next to that item, so the text names the condition and lets the
# player act; it does not order the player about or diagnose their save.

msgid "LOADOUT_REASON_OVER_MASS"
msgstr "Massa acima do limite"

msgid "LOADOUT_REASON_CONTAINER_CYCLE"
msgstr "Contêiner cíclico"

msgid "LOADOUT_REASON_SLOT_NOT_COMPATIBLE"
msgstr "Espaço incompatível"

msgid "LOADOUT_REASON_GRID_OVERLAP"
msgstr "Sobreposição na grade"

msgid "LOADOUT_REASON_OUT_OF_BOUNDS"
msgstr "Fora dos limites"
