msgstr "5,56x45mm M193 (NIJ RF1)"


# ── RESIDUE: DESIGNATIONS, AND THE ONE PLACEHOLDER ──────────────────────────
# Every msgid below has an EMPTY msgstr ON PURPOSE, and the debt counters keep
# counting them on purpose. Both halves of that are deliberate, so here is the
# reasoning in one place.
#
# WHY THEY STAY EMPTY. The debt check is `translate(key) == key` -- it measures
# CHANGE, not presence. These keys are proper nouns: "GOST BR1", "USA AF", "9x18mm
# (GOST BR1)". There is no Portuguese string for them, because in pt-BR they are
# already the right string. Writing an identity msgstr would look like progress in
# the catalogue and change nothing for a player, and writing a paraphrase --
# "GOST BR1 (russo)", "9x18mm (padrão russo)" -- would put words in an item name
# that the game does not have behind them, which is a worse lie than the debt.
#
# WHY THE ENTRY EXISTS AT ALL. Without a block like this the residue reads as 43
# forgotten strings, and the next person to sweep translations will re-derive the
# same conclusion about them that I did: that they were missed. An explicit empty
# msgstr with a comment above it is the record the card asked for ("an explicit
# marker for that key, recorded"), and it is greppable, so the next audit can
# count it instead of re-arguing it.
#
# THE CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly rather than left for someone to discover: the
# DESCRIPTION DEBT note cannot reach 0 and the REGISTRY DEBT note cannot reach 0.
# The reachable floors are 26 of 117 and 19 of 50 as of 2026-09-27, and a
# future run that reports lower is a run that translated a designation.

